---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RelatedArticles from '../../../components/RelatedArticles.astro';
---

<Layout
  type="article"
  title="BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container: is it possible?"
  description="BSL-2 and BSL-3 laboratories in a container: realising the highest biosafety requirements in mobile units. Find out how. Read now."
  canonical="/en/magazine/bsl-2-bsl-3-container-lab"
  ogImage="/images/backgrounds/magazin-bsl-labor.webp"
>
  <div class="pt-20 min-h-screen bg-white">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container: is it possible?",
      "description": "Biosafety levels in container construction are no longer a problem. Find out how we realise the highest biosafety requirements in mobile units.",
      "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Thomas Boss", "url": "https://planexus.de/en/team/thomas-boss", "jobTitle": "Shareholder & Technical Director", "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Planexus GmbH" } },
      "datePublished": "2025-12-20",
      "dateModified": "2025-12-20",
      "image": "/images/backgrounds/magazin-bsl-labor.webp",
      "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Planexus GmbH", "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://planexus.de/images/planexus-logo.png" } }
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://planexus.de/en" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Magazine", "item": "https://planexus.de/en/magazine" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container", "item": "https://planexus.de/en/magazine/bsl-2-bsl-3-container-lab" }
      ]
    })} />

    <section class="relative py-20 bg-slate-900 text-white overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[url('/images/backgrounds/magazin-bsl-labor.webp')] bg-cover bg-center opacity-20"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-900 via-slate-900/90 to-slate-900/70"></div>
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 relative z-10">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
            <span class="bg-primary/20 text-primary px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm font-medium flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2H2v10l9.29 9.29c.94.94 2.48.94 3.42 0l6.58-6.58c.94-.94.94-2.48 0-3.42L12 2Z"/><path d="M7 7h.01"/></svg>
              Safety
            </span>
            <span class="text-gray-400 text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
              15 min read
            </span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold mb-6 leading-tight">
            BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container: is it possible?
          </h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
            Biosafety levels in container construction are no longer a problem. Find out how we realise the highest biosafety requirements in mobile units.
          </p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-6 text-sm text-gray-400">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="4" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="16" x2="16" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="8" x2="8" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="3" x2="21" y1="10" y2="10"/></svg>
              20 December 2025
            </span>
            <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/></svg>
              Thomas Boss, Technical Director, Planexus
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-slate-50 border-b border-gray-100 py-4">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500">
          <a href="/en" class="hover:text-primary">Home</a>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
          <a href="/en/magazine" class="hover:text-primary">Magazine</a>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
          <span class="text-primary font-medium">BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
          <div class="lg:col-span-8">
            <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

              <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
                Work with hazardous biological agents requires the highest safety precautions. Laboratories at biosafety levels BSL-2 and BSL-3 must meet strict structural and technical requirements to protect staff and the environment. For a long time this was regarded as the domain of involved solid construction. Yet modern container laboratories prove: the highest safety is also possible in modular construction.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                Fundamentals of biological biosafety levels
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Biological biosafety levels — known internationally as Biosafety Levels (BSL) — classify laboratories according to the hazard of the organisms handled there. In Germany these are governed by the Biological Agents Ordinance (BioStoffV) and the Technical Rules for Biological Agents (TRBA).
              </p>

              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8 not-prose">
                <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border bg-green-100 text-green-700 border-green-200">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
                    <span class="font-bold">BSL-1</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="font-medium mb-1">Low risk</p>
                  <p class="text-sm opacity-80">Organisms with no known hazard to healthy adults</p>
                </div>
                <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700 border-yellow-200">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
                    <span class="font-bold">BSL-2</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="font-medium mb-1">Moderate risk</p>
                  <p class="text-sm opacity-80">Organisms with moderate hazard potential</p>
                </div>
                <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 border-orange-200">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
                    <span class="font-bold">BSL-3</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="font-medium mb-1">High risk</p>
                  <p class="text-sm opacity-80">Organisms that can cause serious disease</p>
                </div>
                <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border bg-red-100 text-red-700 border-red-200">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
                    <span class="font-bold">BSL-4</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="font-medium mb-1">Highest risk</p>
                  <p class="text-sm opacity-80">Highly hazardous pathogens with no treatment option</p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                While BSL-1 and BSL-2 laboratories are comparatively common, BSL-3 laboratories present a particular challenge because of their complex structural requirements. BSL-4 laboratories — the highest biosafety level for work with pathogens such as Ebola or Marburg virus — have not to date been realised as a container module because of their extreme requirements.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                BSL-2 in container format: proven and reliable
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Laboratories at biosafety level 2 are intended for work with organisms that can cause disease in healthy adults, but for which effective treatment options exist. Typical applications are routine microbiological testing, work with cell cultures or diagnostic laboratories.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The structural requirements for BSL-2 laboratories include, among others:
              </p>

              <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl my-8 not-prose">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
                  BSL-2 requirements
                </h4>
                <ul class="space-y-3">
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Enclosed laboratory area with access control</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Hand-wash basin in the laboratory</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Surfaces that are easy to clean and disinfect</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Windows must be able to remain closed during work</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Suitable biosafety cabinets for aerosol-generating activities</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Decontamination facilities (autoclave in the building)</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Separate protective clothing for the laboratory area</span>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                These requirements can be met without difficulty in a well-planned container module. Our BSL-2 containers are equipped with washable wall surfaces, integrated hand-wash basins and connections for biosafety cabinets. <a href="/en/services/planning" class="text-primary font-medium hover:underline">Technical planning</a> takes all details into account from the start.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-primary/5 border-l-4 border-primary p-6 rounded-r-xl my-8">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                  <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5"/><path d="M9 18h6"/><path d="M10 22h4"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Expert tip: plan in a pass-through autoclave</h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
                      For efficient workflows we recommend integrating a pass-through autoclave. Contaminated materials can then be decontaminated without having to be transported through the clean area. Our <a href="/en/services/equipment" class="text-primary font-medium hover:underline">laboratory equipment experts</a> advise you on the optimal configuration.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                BSL-3: the premier class in container construction
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Laboratories at biosafety level 3 serve work with organisms that can cause serious disease and for which effective therapies or prophylaxes are not always available. These include, for example, Mycobacterium tuberculosis, West Nile virus or certain influenza strains. The structural requirements are correspondingly strict.
              </p>

              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8 not-prose">
                <div class="bg-slate-50 p-5 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
                  <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center text-primary mb-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Access control</h4>
                  <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Multiply secured airlocks with interlock function</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-50 p-5 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
                  <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center text-primary mb-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17.7 7.7a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 1.8 4.3H2"/><path d="M9.6 4.6A2 2 0 1 1 11 8H2"/><path d="M12.6 19.4A2 2 0 1 0 14 16H2"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Negative-pressure holding</h4>
                  <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Permanent negative pressure prevents air escape</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-50 p-5 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
                  <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center text-primary mb-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="8" y2="12"/><line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="16" y2="16"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Gas-tight cabin</h4>
                  <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Fully sealed room envelope</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-50 p-5 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
                  <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center text-primary mb-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><path d="m9 15 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">HEPA filtration</h4>
                  <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Extract filtration with H14 HEPA filters</p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
                The negative-pressure zone: heart of safety
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The most important safety feature of a BSL-3 laboratory is controlled negative-pressure holding. Air pressure in the laboratory area sits about 30 to 50 pascals below ambient pressure. As a result, air flows inwards from outside at every opening — never the reverse. Potentially contaminated air cannot therefore reach the surroundings.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                In a container laboratory this negative-pressure zone is realised by a gas-tight cabin construction. All penetrations — for electrics, media, ventilation — are executed with specialist sealing systems. The ventilation plant is designed redundantly and fitted with automatic emergency shutdown in the event of faults.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-6 rounded-r-xl my-8">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                  <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-amber-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z"/><path d="M12 9v4"/><path d="M12 17h.01"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Important: observe the permit procedure</h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
                      Operation of a BSL-3 laboratory requires a permit under the Biological Agents Ordinance. The approval procedure can take several months. Start preparing early — our <a href="/en/services/consulting" class="text-primary font-medium hover:underline">consulting experts</a> support you in this.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
                The airlock concept
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Access to the BSL-3 area is via a multi-stage airlock system. Typically this consists of a black-and-white separation with changing area, a shower passage and the actual personnel airlock. The airlocks are fitted with interlocks so that both doors can never be opened at the same time.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                In a compact container laboratory this airlock concept must be implemented cleverly. Optimised layouts make it possible to accommodate all required functions in a tight space. Depending on requirements, the airlocks can be housed in a separate upstream container or in the same module.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                Technical systems for maximum safety
              </h2>

              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
                Ventilation and filter systems
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The ventilation plant of a BSL-3 container laboratory is built redundantly. Two independent extract fans ensure continuous operation even if one system fails. Extract air is passed through HEPA filters of class H14, which retain at least 99.995 per cent of all particles with a size of 0.1 to 0.3 micrometres.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Supply air is also filtered to prevent the introduction of contamination. Airflow is designed so that clean air enters in the entrance area and is extracted towards the contamination source — a directed airflow that minimises the spread of aerosols.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-primary/5 border-l-4 border-primary p-6 rounded-r-xl my-8">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                  <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5"/><path d="M9 18h6"/><path d="M10 22h4"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Expert tip: bag-in/bag-out filter housings</h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
                      For safe filter changes we recommend bag-in/bag-out (BIBO) filter housings. These enable contamination-free exchange of HEPA filters without exposing service personnel. Our <a href="/en/services/equipment" class="text-primary font-medium hover:underline">laboratory equipment</a> includes all required safety systems.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
                Decontamination and waste disposal
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                All materials leaving the BSL-3 area must be decontaminated. Pass-through autoclaves are typically used for this, forming the transition between the contaminated and clean areas. Liquid waste is inactivated chemically or thermally before discharge.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                For room gassing — for example after an incident or before maintenance work — connections for formaldehyde evaporators or hydrogen peroxide generators must be provided. These enable complete decontamination of the entire laboratory area.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                Monitoring and documentation
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                A BSL-3 laboratory requires extensive monitoring and documentation systems. Pressure sensors continuously monitor negative-pressure holding and trigger an alarm if there are deviations. Door contacts log every access. Video surveillance documents activities in the laboratory.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl my-8 not-prose">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Our Smart Lab solution for BSL-3 includes:</h4>
                <ul class="space-y-3">
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Continuous differential-pressure measurement with alarm system</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Automatic documentation of all safety-relevant parameters</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Access control with biometric capture</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Video surveillance with recording</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Remote access to status data for authorised persons</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <span class="text-gray-700">Automatic notification to the operations manager in the event of faults</span>
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-200">
                  <a href="/en/services/smart-lab" class="text-primary font-medium hover:underline flex items-center gap-2">
                    Find out more about Smart Lab integration
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
                  </a>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                Advantages of the container concept for high-containment laboratories
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Realising BSL-2 and BSL-3 laboratories in container form offers specific advantages that go beyond the general merits of modular construction:
              </p>

              <div class="bg-primary/5 p-6 rounded-xl my-8 not-prose">
                <ul class="space-y-4">
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <div>
                      <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Controlled manufacture:</span>
                      <span class="text-gray-700 ml-1">The gas-tight cabin is created under workshop conditions with the highest precision — quality levels that would barely be achievable on a construction site.</span>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <div>
                      <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Independence from the existing building:</span>
                      <span class="text-gray-700 ml-1">A container BSL-3 can be installed without involved interventions in existing building structures.</span>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <div>
                      <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Rapid availability:</span>
                      <span class="text-gray-700 ml-1">Realisation time is significantly shorter than for conventional BSL-3 laboratories, which often take years.</span>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <div>
                      <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Flexibility:</span>
                      <span class="text-gray-700 ml-1">If the site changes, the complete laboratory can be moved — the entire certified unit remains intact.</span>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#bbd700" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
                    <div>
                      <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Defined interfaces:</span>
                      <span class="text-gray-700 ml-1">Clear separation between high-containment area and surroundings eases operation and maintenance.</span>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                From concept to approval
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Realisation of a BSL-2 or BSL-3 container laboratory follows a structured process. At the beginning sits the needs analysis: which organisms are to be processed? Which working procedures are planned? How many people will work in the laboratory? On the basis of this information we develop the concept.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                In parallel, coordination with the permitting authorities begins. For BSL-2 laboratories a notification to the competent authority is generally sufficient. BSL-3 laboratories require a permit, the granting of which depends on a review of the structural and organisational prerequisites. Our <a href="/en/services/consulting" class="text-primary font-medium hover:underline">consulting experts</a> accompany you through this process.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white p-8 rounded-2xl my-12 not-prose">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Conclusion: safety and flexibility united</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                  The question “BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container — is it possible?” we can answer with a clear yes. Modern manufacturing technologies and well-thought-out concepts make it possible to realise high-containment laboratories in mobile construction that stand comparison with conventional facilities in every respect. On the contrary: controlled workshop manufacture offers quality advantages, while the flexibility of the container concept opens new fields of use.
                </p>
