    <section class="py-16 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">Frequently asked questions about BSL-2 and BSL-3 container laboratories</h2>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                What is the difference between BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">BSL-2 laboratories work with risk-group 2 pathogens and require a biosafety cabinet, autoclaves and controlled access. BSL-3 laboratories additionally require negative pressure, HEPA filtration, airlocks and gas-tight penetrations. Both levels can be implemented in <a href="/en/services/modular-construction" class="text-primary hover:underline">container construction</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                How long does it take to realise a BSL container laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A BSL-2 container laboratory can be realised within a few months — considerably faster than a conventional new build. BSL-3 projects take somewhat longer because of more complex permit procedures, but are still faster than solid construction. More on the <a href="/en/magazine/lab-container-project-process" class="text-primary hover:underline">project process</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                Which permits do I need for a BSL container laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">For BSL-2 a notification to the competent authority is generally sufficient. BSL-3 requires a permit under the Biological Agents Ordinance (BioStoffV). Building-law permits come on top — all of this is covered in our <a href="/en/magazine/lab-container-permits-building-law" class="text-primary hover:underline">permits guide</a>. Our <a href="/en/services/consulting" class="text-primary hover:underline">consulting</a> accompanies you through the process.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                Can a BSL container laboratory change site?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes, that is one of the great advantages over solid construction. A BSL container laboratory can be dismantled, transported and recommissioned at a new site — the entire certified unit remains intact. More on <a href="/en/services/logistics" class="text-primary hover:underline">logistics &amp; installation</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                What technical equipment belongs in a BSL-2/BSL-3 laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">BSL-2 requires at least biosafety cabinets, autoclaves, eyewash, emergency shower and controlled access. BSL-3 additionally requires HEPA filtration, negative-pressure ventilation systems, gas-tight penetrations and airlocks. Details are in our <a href="/en/magazine/lab-container-equipment-checklist" class="text-primary hover:underline">equipment checklist</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                Is a BSL-3 container laboratory as safe as a conventional one?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes. Modern container laboratories meet exactly the same safety requirements as conventional BSL-3 laboratories. Controlled workshop manufacture even offers quality advantages, because all installations are fitted and tested under optimal conditions.</div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
